  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-3 & =0 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x & =3 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(0.6)=36.869\\,897{\u2026}^{\u2218}\u2248{36.870}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nSince $36.870$ lies inside the range, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={36.870}^{\u2218}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={36.870}^{\u2218}.$\nSince $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={36.870}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/38b2ec0588022556acd825c6b351d572d52034c6ec5cdeddbdff1dbf7baa11a2.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\nX={180}^{\u2218}-{\\theta }_{R}={180}^{\u2218}-{36.870}^{\u2218}={143.130}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nSince this value is already inside the required domain, we keep it as our second solution.\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx\u2248{37}^{\u2218},\\,x\u2248{143}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
